[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2719329543","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104055#issuecomment-2719329543","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104055","id":2719329543,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iFa0H","user":{"login":"ze2j","id":46556066,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTU2MDY2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46556066?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j","html_url":"https://github.com/ze2j","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-12T23:16:19Z","updated_at":"2025-03-12T23:17:49Z","body":"Love it! Very useful in many cases (like to store the neighbors of a cell for example).\r\n\r\n`StaticVector` is usualy the name given to this kind of fixed capacity container. Why not using that name ?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2719329543/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2719335456","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104055#issuecomment-2719335456","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104055","id":2719335456,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iFcQg","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-12T23:21:23Z","updated_at":"2025-03-12T23:24:46Z","body":"> Love it! Very useful in many cases (like to store the neighbors of a cell for example).\r\n> \r\n> `StaticVector` is usualy the name given to this kind of fixed capacity container. Why not using that name ?\r\n\r\nI've seen `Fixed-` used as a prefix for collections where the size is chosen at compile time — hence I chose the name `FixedVector`. \r\nI've not seen `Static` used for this concept. Can you quote some examples?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2719335456/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2719345030","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104055#issuecomment-2719345030","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104055","id":2719345030,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iFemG","user":{"login":"ze2j","id":46556066,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTU2MDY2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46556066?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j","html_url":"https://github.com/ze2j","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-12T23:29:05Z","updated_at":"2025-03-12T23:29:05Z","body":"[Boost static_vector](https://beta.boost.org/doc/libs/1_58_0/doc/html/boost/container/static_vector.html) for example","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2719345030/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2719353103","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104055#issuecomment-2719353103","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104055","id":2719353103,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iFgkP","user":{"login":"ze2j","id":46556066,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NTU2MDY2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46556066?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j","html_url":"https://github.com/ze2j","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ze2j/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-12T23:35:33Z","updated_at":"2025-03-12T23:35:33Z","body":"Could you explain what's the rationale for using placement new instead of a relying on a `std::array<T, CAPACITY>` ? I don't get it. Is to pack the data more efficiently ?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2719353103/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2719362916","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104055#issuecomment-2719362916","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104055","id":2719362916,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iFi9k","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-12T23:43:48Z","updated_at":"2025-03-13T08:12:23Z","body":"> [Boost static_vector](https://beta.boost.org/doc/libs/1_58_0/doc/html/boost/container/static_vector.html) for example\r\n\r\nThat's a good example. I'd like to hear what others think of this alternate name; I don't have a strong preference.\r\n\r\n> Could you explain what's the rationale for using placement new instead of a relying on a `std::array<T, CAPACITY>` ? I don't get it. Is to pack the data more efficiently ?\r\n\r\nOf course! The reason is performance.\r\n\r\nBasically, using `std::array<T, CAPACITY>` will automatically populate the entire array with elements upon construction. For trivial types, like `int`, this is unimportant, and makes no difference.\r\n\r\nFor non-trivial types though, like `Variant`, this would necessitate the whole array to initialize with an initial value (`NULL`). In addition, pushing new objects requires assigning over the old one, which involves branches that account for possible old data. Finally, destruction requires running over all data, even that which wasn't actually used. All waste time.\r\nBy using a raw data array, we can skip these computations for improved efficiency.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2719362916/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2719474471","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104055#issuecomment-2719474471","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104055","id":2719474471,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iF-Mn","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-13T00:59:35Z","updated_at":"2025-03-13T00:59:35Z","body":"No preference on the name—both convey the same general idea","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2719474471/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2720301270","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104055#issuecomment-2720301270","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104055","id":2720301270,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iJIDW","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-13T08:03:37Z","updated_at":"2025-03-13T10:01:29Z","body":"imo something other than static ('Fixed' or any better word we can come up with) is probably better in the name (as I did in 3.x for `FixedArray`) than static as the lifetime usually _isn't_ static.\r\n\r\nIt can either be global/static, or more commonly on the stack. One alternative I suggested in RC was `StackVector`, but for the same reason I wasn't super keen on this, as the lifetime can also be static (although I doubt we'll use this much in Godot). Come to think of it, a `FixedVector` could even be allocated on the heap, so there's that. :grin: \r\n\r\nThis disambiguation is an issue because although we have the basic classification of static (unchanging) & dynamic (changing), in c++ the word (and keyword) `static` is used to refer to objects that have a lifecycle for the entire app.\r\n ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2720301270/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2720417154","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104055#issuecomment-2720417154","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104055","id":2720417154,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iJkWC","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-13T08:44:29Z","updated_at":"2025-03-13T09:00:43Z","body":"Just to throw an idea, I know people *love* STL, but I go by the philosophy of if a routine in a template (or a header in general) can fail, and it returns `void`, return a `bool` instead for success or failure. This will be compiled out if you don't use it, and provides extra info if you want it.\r\n\r\ne.g. `bool push_back(..)`:\r\n```\r\nif (vec.push_back(1))\r\n{\r\n...\r\n}\r\nelse\r\n{\r\n// full\r\n}\r\n```\r\nversus\r\n```\r\nif (!vec.is_full())\r\n{\r\nvec.push_back(1);\r\n}\r\nelse\r\n{\r\n// full\r\n}\r\n```\r\nI guess the second branch in the `push_back` will be compiled out, but I like the emphasis that this can fail. Same with `pop_back()`.\r\n\r\nIncidentally, Grok tells me part of the reason STL `pop_back()` doesn't return success or fail is because it doesn't check for failure, it is UB if you call it on an empty vector. Presumably same for `push_back()`.\r\n\r\nThis of course is an issue with all our containers as we tend to favour \"safe\" versions.\r\n<details>\r\nIn C++, the pop_back() function for containers like std::vector, std::deque, or std::list doesn't return a success or failure indicator because its design assumes a specific contract: it only operates on a non-empty container, and if that contract is met, it will always succeed. This is a deliberate choice rooted in C++'s philosophy of performance, simplicity, and exception handling.\r\n\r\n### Here’s why:\r\n#### Precondition-Based Design:\r\npop_back() is defined with the precondition that the container must not be empty. If you call it on an empty container, it results in undefined behavior (UB) rather than a guaranteed failure state. This avoids the overhead of runtime checks (like returning a success/failure flag) in the common case where the programmer ensures the container isn’t empty. C++ prioritizes \"don’t pay for what you don’t use\"—if you want safety, you’re expected to check empty() or size() beforehand.\r\n\r\n#### Performance Optimization:\r\nAdding a return value (e.g., a bool for success/failure) would introduce additional complexity and potentially cost CPU cycles for something that’s typically unnecessary in well-written code. Since pop_back() is a simple operation (removing the last element and adjusting the size), the standard library avoids burdening it with extra bookkeeping.\r\n\r\n#### Error Handling via Exceptions or Assertions:\r\nC++ prefers mechanisms like exceptions or debug-mode assertions over return codes for error handling. For example, some debug implementations of the standard library (e.g., libstdc++ or MSVC) will trigger an assertion failure if you call pop_back() on an empty container, helping catch bugs during development. In release mode, it’s up to the programmer to avoid UB, aligning with C++’s trust in the developer.\r\n\r\n#### Historical Context and Consistency:\r\nThe STL (Standard Template Library), which influenced C++’s standard containers, was designed by Alexander Stepanov with a focus on generic programming and minimalism. Functions like pop_back() were kept lean and consistent with other operations (e.g., push_back() doesn’t return success either—it either works or throws an exception on allocation failure). Adding a success/failure return would deviate from this established pattern.\r\n\r\n### Alternative: You Can Check Yourself:\r\nIf you need to verify whether pop_back() is safe, you can explicitly check:\r\ncpp\r\n\r\n```\r\nif (!myVector.empty()) {\r\n    myVector.pop_back();\r\n    // Success is guaranteed here\r\n} else {\r\n    // Handle empty case\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis puts the responsibility on the programmer, which is typical in C++’s design.\r\n\r\nContrast this with languages like Java or Python, where methods often return status indicators or throw exceptions for invalid operations. In C++, the choice to omit a success/failure return from pop_back() reflects its low-level, performance-driven ethos. If you really want a \"safe\" version, you could wrap it in a custom function:\r\ncpp\r\n```\r\nbool safe_pop_back(std::vector<int>& vec) {\r\n    if (vec.empty()) return false;\r\n    vec.pop_back();\r\n    return true;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut the standard library doesn’t include this because it assumes you’ll manage the preconditions yourself. Thoughts on this design choice? Does it align with how you approach C++ coding?\r\n</details>","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2720417154/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2720489719","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104055#issuecomment-2720489719","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104055","id":2720489719,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iJ2D3","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-13T09:01:05Z","updated_at":"2025-03-13T09:05:08Z","body":"> Just to throw an idea, I know people _love_ STL, but I go by the philosophy of if a routine in a template (or a header in general) can fail, and it returns `void`, return a `bool` instead for success or failure. This will be compiled out if you don't use it, and provides extra info if you want it.\r\n\r\nThis would definitely be a valid way to handle this!\r\nMy current thinking was that if you push to a `FixedVector` that's lacking space, you _probably_ have a bug on your hand because you didn't make it large enough statically. So a failure would be most appropriate. But I could also see `FixedVector` being used in scenarios where a push against a full vector is reasonable behavior.\r\n\r\nAs for `pop_back()`, I also considered returning the popped `T`, as Rust likes to do. But we don't do this in the codebase elsewhere and it's admittedly less useful than in Rust, which likes to optimize object lifetimes as much as possible. I could also see popping from an empty `FixedVector` returning `bool` (I think I saw that in a library or two as well?), but I think it might more often be a bug we shouldn't ignore, especially in the stack case.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2720489719/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2720515663","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104055#issuecomment-2720515663","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104055","id":2720515663,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6iJ8ZP","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-13T09:10:09Z","updated_at":"2025-03-13T09:10:09Z","body":"> As for pop_back(), I also considered returning the popped T, as Rust likes to do.\r\n\r\nThat's also something I've considered in various forms in the past, although returning a `T` means you have no good options in the case of popping from an empty `vector` (except crashing or returning `T()`).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2720515663/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2746315773","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104055#issuecomment-2746315773","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104055","id":2746315773,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jsXP9","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-23T17:07:32Z","updated_at":"2025-03-23T17:07:32Z","body":"I moved `force_trivial` to the `resize` function only, in accordance to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104522.\r\nIn this PR, it was already used in just `resize`.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2746315773/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2783956312","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104055#issuecomment-2783956312","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104055","id":2783956312,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6l781Y","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-07T16:36:38Z","updated_at":"2025-04-07T16:36:38Z","body":"As ATS mentioned, could you revert the `force_trivial` changes so this can be assessed & integrated as-is? I just realized this was likely kept off the merge queue for that reason, and I'd like to keep this on our radar","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2783956312/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2784245719","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104055#issuecomment-2784245719","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104055","id":2784245719,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6l9DfX","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-07T18:44:24Z","updated_at":"2025-04-07T18:45:49Z","body":"It's still on my radar, just waiting for the next core meeting :) \nI'd very much prefer to keep the template as it is now, so I didn't want to revert until we've discussed it.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2784245719/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2842532998","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104055#issuecomment-2842532998","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104055","id":2842532998,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pbZyG","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-30T16:17:11Z","updated_at":"2025-04-30T16:18:23Z","body":"I've updated the PR according to what was discussed in the core meeting:\r\n- `resize` is removed. Instead, there are two new functions:\r\n- `resize_initialized`, which _always_ initializes new elements, even if they are trivial types.\r\n- `resize_uninitialized`, which _never_ initializes new elements. If the contained type is not trivially destructible, `FixedVector` statically complains for memory safety reasons.\r\n- `force_trivial` is not added to the type as a template parameter. It can be added later if a need for it emerges.\r\n\r\nI believe it's now ready to merge (from my side) :)\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2842532998/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2842570189","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104055#issuecomment-2842570189","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104055","id":2842570189,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pbi3N","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-30T16:27:09Z","updated_at":"2025-04-30T16:27:09Z","body":"One other idea (although not necessary) might be possible to check the alignment in the tests.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2842570189/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2842681332","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104055#issuecomment-2842681332","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104055","id":2842681332,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pb9_0","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-30T17:08:25Z","updated_at":"2025-04-30T17:08:25Z","body":"> One other idea (although not necessary) might be possible to check the alignment in the tests.\r\n\r\nGood idea! Added.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2842681332/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2843415636","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104055#issuecomment-2843415636","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104055","id":2843415636,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pexRU","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-30T21:55:02Z","updated_at":"2025-04-30T21:55:02Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2843415636/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":3,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3478263664","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104055#issuecomment-3478263664","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104055","id":3478263664,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7PUhdw","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-02T20:22:37Z","updated_at":"2025-11-02T22:58:25Z","body":"Wasn't sure where to put this, but from a quick look I found a few places `FixedVector` could potentially be a drop-in replacement for `Vector` and `LocalVector` (except you remove the `resize`s obviously).\r\n\r\nThese are either iterated in-function, or the functions that use them take either a pointer or `Span`.\r\n\r\nIterated in-function:\r\n- `BoneMapping::auto_mapping_process()` (`LocalVector<String>, 5`, one for each hand)\r\n- `SpringBoneCollision3DGizmoPlugin::draw_capsule()` (`Vector3, 4`)\r\n- `SpringBoneCollision3DGizmoPlugin::draw_plane()` (`Vector3, 7`)\r\n- `ImageLoaderHDR::load_image()` (`uint8_t, 128`)\r\n- `SceneCacheInterface::process_simplify_path()` (`uint8_t, 1 + 1 + 4`)\r\n- `TextServerAdvanced::_ensure_cache_for_size()` (`UChar, 255`)\r\n- `AudioStreamPlayer3D::_update_panning()/_calc_reverb_vol()` (`AudioFrame, 4`)\r\n\r\nClass members:\r\n- `NavMap2D/3D.iteration_slots` (`NavMapIteration2D/3D, 2`)\r\n\r\nPassed as `Span` or pointer:\r\n- `BetsyCompressor::_compress()` (`float, 256 * 4`, possibly not safe)\r\n- `RendererSceneCull::_light_instance_update_shadow()` (`Plane, 6`)\r\n\r\nWhile compilation goes fine, these have shown immediate issues in a quick run in Forward+:\r\n- `RendererCanvasRenderRD::RendererCanvasRenderRD()` (`uint8_t, 6 * 2`, made `CanvasItem`s invisible)\r\n- `RendererCompositorRD::initialize()` (`uint8_t, 6 * 2`, turned the whole engine into a big black screen)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3478263664/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]